    "title": "pandas.Interval.overlaps — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1661.gf74cda2e6e documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Interval.overlaps#\n\n- \nInterval.overlaps(*other* )#\n- Check whether two Interval objects overlap. Two intervals overlap if they share a common point, including closed endpoints. Intervals that only have an open endpoint in common do not overlap. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **other** Interval\n    - Interval to check against for an overlap.\n  - Returns:\n    - bool\n    - True if the two intervals overlap.\n See also \n  - `IntervalArray.overlaps`\n  - The corresponding method for IntervalArray.\n  - `IntervalIndex.overlaps`\n  - The corresponding method for IntervalIndex.\n Examples >>> i1 = pd.Interval(0, 2) >>> i2 = pd.Interval(1, 3) >>> i1.overlaps(i2) True >>> i3 = pd.Interval(4, 5) >>> i1.overlaps(i3) False Intervals that share closed endpoints overlap: >>> i4 = pd.Interval(0, 1, closed='both') >>> i5 = pd.Interval(1, 2, closed='both') >>> i4.overlaps(i5) True Intervals that only have an open endpoint in common do not overlap: >>> i6 = pd.Interval(1, 2, closed='neither') >>> i4.overlaps(i6) False",
    "markdown_length": 1011,
